## Location
- /Volumes/Attic/Desktop/Projects/crates/schc/src/compress.rs lines 192-202

## Problem
```rust
Mo::Msb => {
    let bits_to_match = fd.mo_arg.unwrap_or(0) as usize;
    if bits_to_match == 0 || bits_to_match > fd.length_bits as usize {
        return true; // Edge case: match all
    }
    // ...
}
```

When `mo_arg > length_bits` (e.g., trying to match 16 MSBs of an 8-bit field), the function silently returns true (matches all values).

## What Goes Wrong
A misconfigured rule that specifies `mo_arg` larger than the field width will match any value, potentially selecting the wrong compression rule. This fails silently rather than returning an error.

RFC 8724 does not define behavior for this case, but silent acceptance of misconfiguration is a correctness risk.

## Suggested Fix
Return an error or log a warning when `mo_arg > length_bits`:
```rust
if bits_to_match > fd.length_bits as usize {
    return Err(SchcError::InvalidField);
}
```

Alternatively, document the behavior explicitly if "match all" is intentional.
